  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe Sodick Mark 21 post refuses a condition id with one or two digits, for example `C1` or `C2`. The Sodick manuals' examples use these forms. The workaround is to rename the condition to `C001` in the machine file.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe post writes `C1` as `C001` (zero-padded to three digits).\n\n## Evidence (upstream main `eafe6aec6`)\n\n- `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps:322` and `:409`: `/^C[0-9]{3}$/`.\n\nFound by the post audit against the Sodick manuals (#4130).\n\n## Done means\n\n`C1` posts as `C001`. A Mark 21 golden pins it.\n",
